Okay, I'll admit that searching for hidden door, passages, traps, etc. has 
got to be one of my least favorite aspects of any RPG.  So, it's needless to 
say (why do people always preface things they're about to say with that 
phrase?) that I'm getting a bit tired of mashing my "s" key (yeah, I know I 
could type out "n9s", but it hardly seems worth it) when I get to a level 
composed of only three rooms and no down staircase.

I've started out with a Valk since the consensus seems to be that their the 
easiest for newbs to ascend with (+3 shield, Excalibur, and Mjollnir are 
pretty handy for a low-level character), but I'm wondering if my mid-range 
INT & WIS might be holding me back from finding stuff as quickly as I could 
if I was playing a Priest or a Wizard.  Then again, there are all those 
classes with some sort of intrinsic Search ability...

So, here are my questions:

1.  Does INT or WIS (or any other ability) have a direct effect on how many 
times I have to hit the (s)earch key to find things?
2.  How exactly does the intrinsic Search ability of some classes work? 
(e.g. Does it automatically do a free (s)earch each turn or maybe even "n5s" 
or better?  Does it just have a fixed chance of revealing anything hidden 
the first time you encounter an area?)
3.  Do items that grant a Search ability work the same way as the class 
intrinsic Search ability?
4.  Ditto for monster corpses that you can eat?
5.  Any other way I might not have thought of that could save me some 
time/keystrokes? 



